{
  "name": "Black Stair L13: Reverse Crossing",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-symbol-reverse-blue.webp",
  "system": {
    "category": "technique",
    "source": "Bad Eden Bulwark + Shadow Courier v1.0 (RFI-native rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>The door you came through is also the door you can leave through.</em></p><p>You may use your class's <strong>The Crossing</strong> ability to <strong>leave</strong> a location you should not be able to leave. This includes:</p><ul><li><p>Prisons, oubliettes, sealed rooms</p></li><li><p>Dimensional traps and pocket planes</p></li><li><p>Banishment effects targeting you</p></li><li><p>Political or ritual exile bound to a specific place</p></li></ul><p>You may bring up to <strong>your Initiation tier</strong> willing allies along (1 at T1, 2 at T2, 3 at T3, 4 at T4 — note this feature unlocks at T3, so you can always bring at least 3).</p><p>You arrive at <strong>a location you have personally visited before</strong>. The destination is a player choice from your previously-visited locations, with GM right of refusal for narrative impossibilities.</p><p><strong>Limit:</strong> Reverse Crossing cannot be used to escape an active combat round (you must be out of initiative). It still consumes The Crossing's 1/scene use.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
